What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/active
Date:		May 2025
KernelVersion:	6.15
Contact:	qat-linux@intel.com
Description:
		(RO) This attribute provides information about the currently active
		Secure Version Number (SVN) for the Anti-Rollback (ARB) feature.

		The Anti-Rollback feature prevents downgrades to older firmware versions
		on the Acceleration Device. This read-only attribute allows users to
		query the SVN of the currently active firmware. When reading the file,
                anticipate a non-zero integer as the result.

		Example usage::

			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/active
			2

		This attribute is only available for devices that support the
		Anti-Rollback (ARB) feature.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/commit
Date:		May 2025
KernelVersion:	6.15
Contact:	qat-linux@intel.com
Description:
		(WO) This attribute allows users to trigger the commit operation for
		the Anti-Rollback (ARB) feature on the Acceleration Device.

		The Anti-Rollback feature commits the currently active firmware SVN as the
		authorized version, preventing future downgrades to firmware with a
		lower SVN. Depending on configuration of ARB the commit action can be
		ephemeral or persistent.

		Before committing the SVN update, it is crucial to check the current values
		of Active SVN (`active`) Enforced Min SVN (`enforced_min`) and Permanent
		MIN SVN (`permanent_min`). This verification helps ensure that the commit
		operation aligns with the intended outcome.

		While writing to the file, any value other than '1' will result in an error.
		Therefore, it is advisable to use this attribute with caution, only when it
		is necessary to commit firmware SVN.

		Example usage::

 			## Steps
 			## 1. Check current values of enforced_min, permanent_min and active SVN.
 			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/enforced_min
 			2
 			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/permanent_min
 			2
 			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/active
 			3

			## 2. Start commit operation
			# echo 1 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/commit
	 		## 3. Check updated values of enforced_min and permanent_min
 			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/enforced_min
 			3
 			## This will only be updated if ARB is configured as persistent
 			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_svn/permanent_min
 			3

		This attribute is only available for devices that support the
		Anti-Rollback (ARB) feature.
